  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3460",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3460: Important priority package update for ghostscript",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-17 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-17 23:01:03"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-112922:\n\tA flaw was found in Ghostscript. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by enticing a user to process a specially crafted PDF or PostScript document containing malicious mesh shading data. Due to improper bounds validation during the processing of indexed color values, Ghostscript triggers an out-of-bounds memory read. Successful exploitation can lead to a Denial of Service (DoS) through an application crash or result in limited information disclosure.\n\nCVE-2026-110133:\n\tA flaw was found in Ghostscript. When processing a specially crafted TrueType font or document embedding one, an accounting error during font rendering can bypass buffer size checks, triggering a heap-based buffer overflow. A remote attacker could exploit this by enticing a victim or automated service to open the malicious content, potentially resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS) crash or arbitrary code execution.\n",
